WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.416
A flowering plant has four main
parts. Each part has a job to do.

2
00:00:09.636 --> 00:00:13.490
You will find out what each part
does, and what a plant needs.

3
00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.845
Here is a whole flowering plant.
Let us start under the soil.

4
00:00:18.065 --> 00:00:21.733
These are the roots. They
anchor the plant in the soil.

5
00:00:21.953 --> 00:00:25.158
They hold it so well that
the wind cannot blow it over.

6
00:00:25.378 --> 00:00:28.814
The roots also take in water
and minerals from the soil.

7
00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:32.796
This is the stem. It holds the
plant up towards the light.

8
00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:36.452
The stem carries that water
to every leaf and flower.

9
00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:42.247
These are the leaves. They are wide and
flat, to catch as much light as they can.

10
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:45.903
They catch sunlight and use
it to make the plant's food.

11
00:00:46.123 --> 00:00:49.560
Roots do not eat soil. The
food is made in the leaves.

12
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.727
This is the flower. Its
bright petals attract insects.

13
00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:57.059
The flower makes seeds, so
there can be new plants.

14
00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:00.994
A flower is one part of a
plant, not the whole plant.

15
00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:06.184
A plant needs water and light. It
also needs the right temperature.

16
00:01:06.404 --> 00:01:10.769
Today you will keep one plant warm
and put one somewhere very cold.

17
00:01:10.989 --> 00:01:14.240
Both plants get the same
water and the same light.

18
00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.943
What will happen to the
cold plant after five days?

19
00:01:18.163 --> 00:01:21.600
Say what you think first. What
you think is your prediction.

20
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.654
Only one thing changes: the temperature.

21
00:01:24.874 --> 00:01:28.636
The water and the light stay
the same. That is a fair test.

22
00:01:28.856 --> 00:01:32.710
Day after day, the warm plant
stays healthy and green.

23
00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.738
By day five the cold plant
has drooped and gone yellow.

24
00:01:37.238 --> 00:01:41.046
Write down what you saw. A
table keeps your results tidy.

25
00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:44.889
One row for the warm plant.
One row for the cold plant.

26
00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:51.471
Warm plant: healthy and green.
Cold plant: drooping and yellow.

27
00:01:51.971 --> 00:01:55.825
Now a scientist asks two
questions about the results.

28
00:01:56.045 --> 00:02:00.364
The first is this. Did the
results support my prediction?

29
00:02:00.584 --> 00:02:03.649
You predicted the cold plant
would droop, and it did.

30
00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:08.606
The second question is what the
results tell you. That is a conclusion.

31
00:02:08.826 --> 00:02:12.820
Plants need the right temperature,
as well as water and light.

32
00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.710
Roots take in water. The stem
carries it to the leaves.

33
00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:20.367
Leaves make the food, and
the flower makes the seeds.

34
00:02:20.587 --> 00:02:23.838
A plant needs water, light
and the right temperature.

35
00:02:24.058 --> 00:02:27.726
You predicted, you tested, you
wrote it down, and you concluded.
